# Files the tests WRITE. `test_the_ground_label_survives_a_save_and_load` makes
# `ground_rt.hxw`; `tests/sections.loft` makes several `sections_*.hxw`.
#
# ⚠ NOT a blanket `*.hxw`, which it was until 2026-08-03. `presection.hxw` is a
# COMMITTED FIXTURE — bytes written by the writer as it stood before sections
# existed — and it is the one file here that must not be regenerable, because its
# whole job is to be a world the current code did not produce. A blanket rule
# would have left it untracked and the gate would have passed on every machine
# that happened to have run the generator.
ground_rt.hxw
sections_*.hxw
